          "intro": "Lincoln charges for the cathedral, and the castle's wall walk, prison and Magna Carta vault are ticketed, but the castle grounds themselves are free, which surprises most visitors. The city museum has been shut for redevelopment since 2024. This route walks the free city instead, from the river up through Steep Hill to the Roman gate at the top. About 1.9 km, and it is uphill nearly all the way: Steep Hill is exactly what its name says and is not suitable if you have limited mobility. Two stops are free to go inside, and read the days: they overlap on Fridays and Saturdays all year, with Mondays added outside the winter months. The walk covers about 1.9 km and takes roughly 25–35 minutes at an easy pace, not counting time spent at each stop.",
