          "intro": "Liverpool spent the nineteenth century as one of the world's great ports and built accordingly, then spent the twentieth losing the trade and rebuilding anyway. This route runs from the dock warehouses up through the civic quarter to two cathedrals at the top of the hill. Be warned: at 5 km with a steady climb at the end, it is the longest walk in this collection. Almost every stop is free. Note the opening days before you go: some stops on this route close on Mondays and others on Sundays, so a weekday between the two is the safest choice. The walk covers about 5.0 km and takes roughly 64–74 minutes at an easy pace, not counting time spent at each stop.",
