          "intro": "This is the ceremonial half-mile of Britain: the monarch's house at one end, Parliament at the other, and the government offices strung between them. Almost all of it is free to see, and the walk finishes at one of the great free galleries in the world. About 3 km, flat throughout. The walk covers about 2.9 km and takes roughly 37–47 minutes at an easy pace, not counting time spent at each stop.",
