          "intro": "Manchester has the best free museums of any city in this collection: six buildings on this route can be walked into for nothing. But read the days before you set off. The John Rylands Library opens Wednesday to Saturday only, the Art Gallery closes on Mondays, the People's History Museum on Tuesdays and the Central Library on Sundays, so the one window when every indoor stop is open together is Wednesday to Saturday. About 3.1 km, flat, city-centre pavements throughout. The walk covers about 3.1 km and takes roughly 40–50 minutes at an easy pace, not counting time spent at each stop.",
