          "sample": "Start at the city's art gallery, which states on its own site that entry is free, donations are welcome and booking is not needed. Read that carefully though: named exhibitions carry an admission charge, so free means the permanent collection and most of what is on. The strength here is British art, with a good Pre-Raphaelite holding and a room of northern painters, and the building itself is Edwardian with a handsome top-lit hall. There is a café on the ground floor in a large room hung with pictures, and a play space for children. It opens ten until half past four and is closed on Sundays. An hour is enough; two if you sit. It stands on New Bridge Street a few minutes from the Monument, so it is an easy start whether you arrive by Metro or train.",
