          "intro": "Mykonos is famous for things that cost money, and this route deliberately covers the things that do not. The old town's irregular maze of lanes is traditionally said to have helped confuse raiders arriving from the sea, although its development was not the result of a single documented plan. The five stops run west through it from the harbour square to the windmills on the ridge. Everything is free. The route is short, mostly level, and paved throughout with stone that is uneven in places, with a short climb at the end up to the windmill ridge, which is exposed and windy. Two of the stops are exteriors only. Like everywhere on this island, it is far quieter before the middle of the morning.",
