          "sample": "Start at the Ulster Museum, which is free and is the single best thing on this walk. Five floors run from dinosaur bones and Egyptian material through applied art and painting to the Troubles and Beyond gallery. Reviewers who have seen a lot of museums rate it very highly and give the same warning: it is large, it closes at five, and you should decide in advance what you want rather than trying to see everything. Closed on Mondays. An hour to ninety minutes fits this route; reviewers who came for the museum alone quote two to three. The permanent Troubles and Beyond gallery approaches this contested history through objects and accounts representing multiple perspectives. The Spanish Armada material comes from the Girona, wrecked off the Antrim coast in 1588, and the gold recovered from it is here. The museum is part of National Museums NI and the building itself is a brutalist extension grafted onto a 1929 classical front, which reviewers either like or do not.",
