          "intro": "Cork is built on an island in the River Lee with hills on both sides, and the centre is small enough to cross on foot in twenty minutes. For the complete route, walk Tuesday through Saturday. The English Market is closed on Sundays and bank holidays, while Elizabeth Fort is closed on Mondays from October through April. Saint Fin Barre's Cathedral and Saint Anne's Shandon both charge for their interiors, but their exteriors can be viewed free of charge. There is one climb, up to Shandon at the end. The walk covers about 1.8 km and takes roughly 24–34 minutes at an easy pace, not counting time spent at each stop.",
