          "name": "Santiago de Compostela",
          "tagline": "The Cathedral Is Free",
          "intro": "The thing worth knowing before you arrive: the cathedral itself is free, every day of the year, from seven in the morning until nine at night, or half past eight on summer Saturdays. So is the tomb of the Apostle. What costs money is the museum, the Crypt of the Pórtico and the roof tour: not the building, and the Pórtico de la Gloria has limited free tickets of its own. Add a free Renaissance cloister, a market, and a park with the classic view of the towers, and this is among the cheapest great cities in Spain. This is the shortest route in the collection, and it runs gently uphill at the end into the park. The market and the free Fonseca cloister both close on Sundays. The walk covers about 1.3 km and takes roughly 16–26 minutes at an easy pace, not counting time spent at each stop.",
