          "name": "Toledo",
          "tagline": "Three Free Windows on One Hill",
          "intro": "Almost everything inside Toledo's walls charges, and yet three of its ticketed interiors open free if you time them right. The cathedral opens its naves free on weekday mornings, last entry a quarter past nine. The Sephardic Museum in the Tránsito synagogue is free from two on Saturdays and all day Sunday. The Army Museum in the Alcázar is free on Wednesdays. They do not combine. Saturday afternoon and Sunday get you the synagogue. Wednesday can get you both the cathedral and the Army Museum, but not in the mapped order: you would take the cathedral's early window first, then walk back up to the Alcázar when it opens at ten, which means leaving this sequence and adding a few hundred metres of backtracking that the 2.7 km total does not include. About 2.7 km, entering at the north gate and leaving by the western bridge. The route climbs from the Puerta de Bisagra through Zocodover to the Alcázar, then trends downhill through the Judería before a steeper final descent to the bridge. The walk covers about 2.7 km and takes roughly 35–45 minutes at an easy pace, not counting time spent at each stop.",
